<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifd3fd1c8063db97b3f1fe057ace82d22def76943" commit="c0adc477fb1059da1858fe74662f6cb657f6e359" commit_message="minigbm: Fix cursor and scanout flags  We were incorrectly advertising the scanout and cursor flags in the drivers.  Chrome never used the BO_USE_CURSOR flag (see chromium:666488), and we set it for incorrect formats.  Let's only advertise ARGB8888/XRGB8888 cursors if they were previously advertised, and prevent cursors from being used as render targets.  For scanout, formats can vary from kernel version to kernel version. For example, the v3.18 i915 driver can't scanout NV12, but the upstream v4.4 i915 driver can.  Let's query the KMS API in those cases.  In addition, we would also like to move to a place where our backends can determine if a specific {format, usage, format modifier} tuple is supported. The plan is to add modifiers to the properties that are exposed in KMS, which can help with optimization.  BUG=b:31942635, chromium:666488 TEST=Ran graphics_Gbm and checked if Chrome boots on cyan, minnie, and nyan_big  CQ-DEPEND=CL:413325  Change-Id: Ifd3fd1c8063db97b3f1fe057ace82d22def76943 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405019 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405019" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/19/405019/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia9f3bb471539c5af8c71003595464046b1d7209f" commit="0784ea27bf2eb51addf42300bf411a66f575aa22" commit_message="minigbm: rename mutex  The mutex also protects the driver supported linked list, so it's a misnomer to call it &quot;table_lock&quot;.  BUG=none TEST=minigbm builds  CQ-DEPEND=CL:405019  Change-Id: Ia9f3bb471539c5af8c71003595464046b1d7209f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414584 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414584" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/84/414584/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9417caff22ea66e4179fe41d534d8cb9510ef7a3" commit="1273184834506f093e7195b9c0ce7cd953909c13" commit_message="minigbm: rename DRV_BO_USE_* to BO_USE_*  It's somewhat easier to read.  BUG=none TEST=minigbm still builds  CQ-DEPEND=CL:405019  Change-Id: I9417caff22ea66e4179fe41d534d8cb9510ef7a3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414585 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414585" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/85/414585/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7ea9261abf667c912f24fa8498247693d39bff30" commit="0110b3b63c67e353346a0c48e79648ad0a6c752f" commit_message="Remove kevin-tpm2 builder config  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I7ea9261abf667c912f24fa8498247693d39bff30 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414255 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414255" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/55/414255/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie911294b718d7603cafe722c9b809736d2336608" commit="1fdcab84a4d28c70914d71e358e8eddbaf654911" commit_message="instalog: implement plugin store  Implement a plugin &quot;store&quot;.  Usage: From within a plugin, self.store can be accessed and modified at any time.  In order to save the store to disk, self.SaveStore() should be called.  The next time Instalog is started, the last-saved store will be restored.  In order to inspect a plugin store, the CLI &quot;inspect&quot; command should be used:  ./instalog inspect [-h] plugin_id [json_path]  positional arguments:   plugin_id   ID of plugin to inspect   json_path   path of store JSON to print  json_path uses a simplified version of jq's JSON querying language to select information out of the dictionary. The supported operators are &quot;.&quot; and &quot;[]&quot;.  Example:  {'hello': {'world': [100, 200]}}  &quot;.hello.world[0]&quot; ==&gt; 100 &quot;.hello.world&quot;    ==&gt; [100, 200] &quot;.&quot;               ==&gt; {'hello': {'world': [100, 200]}}  Additional change: Remove GetStateDir from CoreAPI.  BUG=b:32271891 TEST=Manually on local machine  Change-Id: Ie911294b718d7603cafe722c9b809736d2336608 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412307 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412307" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/07/412307/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I564c221051424943e753c928ab2708031a66af59" commit="dee0981f0c117bc3b88edc2665813ef32fc427c4" commit_message="instalog: implement flush command for output plugins  Implement output plugin &quot;flush&quot; functionality.  This CLI command will wait until an output plugin processes all pending events before returning, up until the timeout provided.  Using the command will exit with error code 0 on success, and 1 on failure, also printing an explanation to stdout.  Example:   $ ./instalog flush --timeout 5 stdout   Flushed `stdout' successfully (1221169 / 1221169 events)  CLI command specification is as follows:   ./instalog flush [-h] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [plugin_id]    positional arguments:     plugin_id             ID of plugin to flush    optional arguments:     -h, --help            show this help message and exit     --timeout TIMEOUT, -w TIMEOUT                           time to wait before giving up  BUG=b:32271891 TEST=Manually on local machine  Change-Id: I564c221051424943e753c928ab2708031a66af59 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413087 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="413087" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/87/413087/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaa6033e7b27498be01102fcd2f61df67b195f79d" commit="3d03d6148dab952918621fc16d3fe419e49b11fb" commit_message="cheets_CTSHelper: add to suite:smoke.  This adds the simplest possible Android test to the VM.  BUG=b:31838505 TEST=None. (cq will do it)  Change-Id: Iaa6033e7b27498be01102fcd2f61df67b195f79d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414635 Commit-Ready: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="414635" owner_email="ihf@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/35/414635/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0de70ec798b8da77da1d53b0297fe217ee935155" commit="afa9b2038ef81d8797d5526312719d08d49d6c5e" commit_message="trunks: add 'open' to seccomp filters  When an error is detected in TpmUtility::CheckState(), trunksd crashes when minijail blocks 'open' syscall. Can be seen on the simulator, where there is no firmware to initialize the TPM.  BUG=chromium:669109 TEST=Start on the simulator, no &quot;blocked syscall: open&quot; in logs.  Change-Id: I0de70ec798b8da77da1d53b0297fe217ee935155 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414952 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="414952" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="aosp/platform/system/tpm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/tpm" ref="refs/changes/52/414952/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I69e151549ddcd784b310e2e5fc6d2d1956d9c529" commit="30ecd00981dce09c8cff2638b1a0d302e3820499" commit_message="cros-kernel2: Remove unused wireless variant 3.16  Use flag for 'wireless316' is not referenced by any build. Remove this variant from the use flags here, and in a different CL, remove the corresponding stack from the 3.14 kernel.  Having unused wireless stacks creates a lot of confusion while adding new code or debugging, and has extra overhead while backporting patches.  BUG=chromium:663832 TEST=None  Change-Id: I69e151549ddcd784b310e2e5fc6d2d1956d9c529 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413023 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="413023" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/23/413023/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic34f1de735df75f795a31ebbced76f77e0d4f8b5" commit="c73dee230163a31fc705ff14dcd905d08ae5a994" commit_message="goofy: move TestListIterator into a separate file  Since goofy.py is the entry point of factory toolkit, class in this file will be __main__.XXX rather than cros.factory.goofy.goofy.XXX.  This will cause problem when we are serializing and deserializing the objects.  Move TestListIterator into a separate file to prevent this issue.  BUG=b:32721069 TEST=goofy/goofy_unittest.py, goofy/test_list_iterator_unittest.py  Change-Id: Ic34f1de735df75f795a31ebbced76f77e0d4f8b5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412499 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412499" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/99/412499/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I364e60d4bffc913439086f58c88d6ca12217eadc" commit="867cbc2ed1cce110e1463311313e7b383324787a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: wireless: Remove unused wireless-3.16 stack  Chrome OS products based on 3.14 kernel fall into 3 categories:  (1) Ones with Intel wifi chipset (WP2) - (Auron/Jecht family, samus) (2) Ones with Marvell (8897) or Broadcom chipset - (veyron family)  Both of these use wireless-3.8, ie. the wireless stack provided by drivers/net/wireless-3.8/ and net/wireless-3.8/  (3) Jetstream family - uses wireless-4.2 (whirlwind, arkham) or wireless-3.18 (storm, whirlwind testbed) stacks,  This commit removes the following unused stack from 3.14 kernel:   drivers/net/wireless-3.16/   include/wireless-3.16/   net/mac80211-3.16/   net/wireless-3.16/  Having unused wireless stacks around in the kernel creates confusion in code search while adding new code or debugging, and has extra overhead while backporting patches.  BUG=chromium:663832 TEST=Launched build trybots for samus, veyron_minnie, auron_paine  Change-Id: I364e60d4bffc913439086f58c88d6ca12217eadc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414233 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="414233" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/414233/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I4cee7efd0652014dadd14d03dd10354fc309419d" commit="480f68449b99df6542f37ad81e0f8dd5b89a3688" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Renormalize splitconfig  The 3.8 kernel has not had configs normalized in a while, fix that in order to make new config changes smooth and similar to the newer kernels.  Ran ./chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig and hit return for inquiries.  Major changes that show up here should be due: *  fc3631dbd3a5  (&quot;CHROMIUM: config: Remove FBDEV&quot;)    - for CONFIG_FB_* and possibly CONFIG_DRM* changes  *  17eb18f8e9c3 (&quot;CHROMIUM: config: Enable traffic shaping modules&quot;)    - for CONFIG_IFB, CONFIG_NET_ACT* changes  *  6d72900c3d07 (&quot;MALI: r12p0-04rel0 kbase&quot;)    - for *MALI* configs  Change-Id: I4cee7efd0652014dadd14d03dd10354fc309419d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415025 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="415025" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/25/415025/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I16cee3d20fd157a13514664fb6e31202f9a6229a" commit="0045b400039e56af5da38de095e88310c2a76d54" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: wireless: Remove unused wireless-3.8 stack  Chrome OS products based on 3.18 kernel fall into 3 categories:  (1) Ones with Intel wifi chipset (StP2) (2) Ones with Marvell (8897) wifi chipset  Both of these use wireless/, ie. the wireless stack provided by drivers/net/wireless/ and net/wireless/  (3) Gale (from the Jetstream family) - uses wireless-4.2  This commit removes the following unused stack from 3.18 kernel:   drivers/net/wireless-3.8/   include/wireless-3.8/   net/mac80211-3.8/   net/wireless-3.8/  The example comment in net/Kconfig is modified to mention wireless-4.2 instead of wireless-3.8, as that is the only supported alternate stack on this kernel, as of this commit.  Having unused wireless stacks around in the kernel creates confusion in code search while adding new code or debugging, and has extra overhead while backporting patches.  BUG=chromium:663832 TEST=None  Change-Id: I16cee3d20fd157a13514664fb6e31202f9a6229a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413006 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="413006" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/06/413006/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I4404762f8d7d39dc15ab8c382e4e13804c6b9d30" commit="9f2c003184dcdeaddb57020010348cc09480ff64" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: wireless: Remove unused wireless-3.4 stack  Chrome OS products based on 3.10 kernel fall into two categories: (a) Ones with Intel wifi chipset (WP2) - (Rambi family) (b) Ones with Marvell wifi chipset (8897) - (Nyan family) Both of these use the wireless38 use flag, ie. the wireless stack provided by drivers/net/wireless-3.8/ and net/wireless-3.8/  This commit removes the following unused stack from 3.10 kernel:   drivers/net/wireless-3.4/   include/wireless-3.4/   net/mac80211-3.4/   net/wireless-3.4/  Having unused wireless stacks around in the kernel creates confusion in code search while adding new code or debugging, and has extra overhead while backporting patches.  BUG=chromium:663832 TEST=None  Change-Id: I4404762f8d7d39dc15ab8c382e4e13804c6b9d30 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414549 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414549" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesou